# ---- Build artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
/target
**/*.rs.bk
# The vault fixture is a real crate (the eval harness's mutation-validity gate
# runs `cargo check` over every mutant of it). Its build output is not ours to
# commit; its Cargo.lock is, so the gate resolves the same dependency tree in
# CI as it does locally.
/tests/fixtures/programs/*/target

# ---- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY is read from the environment (crates/dike-core/src/llm/).
# Never commit it; never log it; never put it in a report.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Corpus: fetched content is NOT ours to redistribute ----------------
# Spec §7: audit reports are published, not public-domain. We commit the
# manifest (corpus/sources.toml) and the fetch code; never the fetched text.
# corpus/notes/ IS committed — those are our own derived notes.
/corpus/cache
/corpus/index
/corpus/.sources.toml.tmp.*

# ---- Local retrieval stores ---------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# ---- Agent scaffolding --------------------------------------------------
# SDD task briefs, implementer reports and the run ledger. Working state for
# AI-assisted development, not project history. Durable decisions from it are
# distilled into docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md — keep that current instead.
/.superpowers

# ---- Editor / OS --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
/.idea

# ---- Profiling / coverage ----------------------------------------------
*.profraw
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg
